                <pb facs="1057" n="1031" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg1031"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">396.1 GE/6–454: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The United States Delegation to the Department of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-06-04T15:00:00+01:00">June 4, 1954—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Secto 374. Repeated information Saigon 142, Paris 384. Dac Khe told Heath
                    yesterday that he had protested to French delegation that French Officers, who
                    have now started talks in Geneva with representatives of Viet Minh command, are
                    defeatists. Vietnamese Government has Colonel Kim sitting in on these talks and
                    Vietnamese delegation has added Tran Van Tuyen, both of whom have been
                    instructed watch for any signs of “defeatist concessions” by their French
                    colleagues.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
